+### Docker service socket recovery
+
+If Docker's authoritative startup log reports it cannot remove its
+`Docker/run/dockerInference`, `Docker/run/dockerEthernetVfkit`,
+`Docker/run/userAnalyticsOtlpHttp.sock`, or
+`docker-secrets-engine/engine.sock` socket,
+quit Docker Desktop cleanly first.
+`host docker-socket-repair --socket ABSOLUTE_PATH --dry-run` verifies
+all Desktop backend processes have exited and the exact target is a zero-byte
+Windows AF_UNIX socket. Apply with `--confirm` repeats those checks and renames
+the socket in place to a timestamped quarantine name. It preserves the socket
+for diagnosis and leaves Desktop stopped. Restart Desktop normally afterward.
+
+### Docker data disk adoption
+
+For a fresh offline copy, use `host docker-disk copy --source ABSOLUTE_VHDX
+--destination NEW_ABSOLUTE_VHDX --dry-run`. Apply with `--confirm` preserves
+the source, refuses an existing destination, checks available disk space,
+streams the copy while hashing the source, then independently reads and hashes
+every destination byte. A SHA-256 mismatch or changing source prevents final
+installation. Partial copies remain available for diagnosis. `--output PATH.json`
+retains the verification record. Docker stays stopped throughout.
+
+When Docker Desktop leaves a completed WSL disk copy after a failed move,
+`host docker-disk adopt` can select the existing copy offline. Stop all managed
+workloads, then stop Docker Desktop cleanly before previewing this command:
+
+```powershell
+anvil-serving host docker-disk adopt --source C:\Docker\wsl\disk\docker_data.vhdx --destination D:\Docker\DockerDesktopWSL\disk\docker_data.vhdx --settings C:\DockerSettings\settings-store.json --dry-run
+```
+
+The command supports the inspected Docker settings schema 45. It verifies
+matching VHD identifiers, virtual capacity and file sizes, repeats the disk
+identity and detached-state checks, and refuses while Docker Desktop processes
+remain. Apply with `--confirm` creates an exact settings backup and changes only
+the WSL storage root. Both disk files remain, and Docker stays stopped.
+
+Matching metadata does not prove byte identity or application consistency.
+After restart, verify the destination is attached, the source is detached,
+and cache inventory and managed workloads are healthy before retiring the
+source. The result reports `configured-pending-restart` until that independent
+verification is performed. To roll back, stop Desktop cleanly and restore the
+reported settings backup before restarting with the retained original disk.
+
